desc:
Shipped as PR #81 (squash e75f157). The `outlines` member was a STREAM carrying the whole corpus in every frame, with the fine-grained part delegated to a client-side `reconcile` keyed on a Solid default the payload never promised. It is now a COLLECTION keyed by root-relative file path — declared in the protocol as `keySchema` — served with the batched `deltas` verb: the whole keyed set on (re)subscribe, then one coalesced {upserts, removes} frame per probe tick. Wire cost is O(changed files), so a `git pull` that rewrites forty outlines is still one frame.

@olai/store keeps the diff it already computed: a published Snapshot names `changed` and `removed`, so a consumer publishing per file does not re-derive it by comparing two whole snapshots. It spans the gap between two PUBLISHED revisions rather than one probe — a probe the codec refuses publishes nothing, so what it found is still owed to the next revision that validates, and a path edited-then-deleted is a remove rather than a change. Still no olai types in the package: it is path talk.

@olai/surface declares OutlineEntry — a file's nodes, its `rev`, and its `broken`, which is the per-entity error scope as DATA: an unreadable file keeps its key and carries its errors — plus a `manifest` cell for the set-wide facts, whose `null` is the "never loaded" bit a collection cannot express (an empty snapshot means the directory holds no outlines; a first probe still running has to say something else).

The server cuts one revision into entries and maps the store's changed/removed onto the collection's verbs (server/src/outlines.ts), published by one owned fiber so a revision's entries and manifest are one write. The client's read side is one module (web/src/client/outlines.ts): the collection's keys in path order are the sidebar's list, and `derive` over every entry's nodes is the one derivation the whole app reads.

docs/brainstorming/outlines-as-collection.md moves from brainstorming to BUILT, with its open questions answered.

Original filing: Re-model the `outlines` stream as a surface collection keyed by file path, with the opt-in deltas verb: snapshot on (re)subscribe, then one coalesced {upserts, removes} frame per probe tick — wire cost O(changed files) instead of O(corpus), keying declared in the protocol (keySchema) rather than inherited from a client-library default, per-entity brokenness as plain entry data. The store's probe already computes the change list; expose it as a per-publish summary so the patch computation stays encapsulated in packages/store. Timing open: bundle with the kolu writeWrappedValue fix (same client layer), or wait until corpus size makes full-snapshot frames hurt; also pushes the frame-cap horizon out.
